    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0145" n="125" xml:id="pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC/9–348:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-03T20:00:00-06:00">September 3,
                            1948—8 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1061. Foreign Minister stated tonight, after expressing appreciation of friendly
                    and other implications of Deptel 847, August
                        26<anchor n="1" xml:id="d72-f1"/> that Mexico is not interested in election
                    to UNSC. He stated some restlessness has become
                    apparent on part of other Latin American states over repeated occupation by
                    larger Latin American states of important UN
                    posts. He added that Mexico’s principal aspiration at moment is to obtain place
                    on Economic and Social Council at expiration her present term on Trusteeship
                    Council.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
